---
title: Tahini Flapjacks
author: Jonathan Simmonds
servings: 8
cook time: 25 minutes
---

Combine @porridge oats{100%g} and @jumbo oats{100%g} and toast in a #baking sheet{} at 160°C for ~{10%minutes}.

Combine @sesame oil{50%g}, @dark chocolate{40%g}, @tahini{100%g}, and @honey{50%g} in a #small saucepan{} and gently warm until the chocolate is melted.

Mash @banana{1}(ripe) in a large bowl (if not ripe enough add to the hot oven).

Add @ground cardamom{3%tsp}, @ground ginger{1%tsp}, and the melted chocolate to the mashed banana and mix together.

Slowly add the oats, nuts, and seeds, stirring regularly.

Firmly press into a lined baking tin and bake at 160°C for ~{20-25%minutes}.
